 "final_text": "All six fields recorded. Summary of the brief for Robin:\n\n**Caterpillar Inc. (CAT) \u2014 Leverage & Relationship Check**\n\n| Year | LT Debt | Equity (incl. NCI) | LT D/E |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2022 | $25,714M | $15,891M | **1.6181** |\n| 2023 | $24,472M | $19,503M | **1.2548** |\n| 2024 | $27,351M | $19,494M | **1.4030** |\n\n- **3-yr average (of yearly ratios, per policy):** **1.4253**\n- **Classification (TRS-POL-011, latest FY alone \u2192 FY2024 = 1.40):** **moderate** \u2014 standard terms, annual review (band is 1.0\u20133.0 inclusive; over-levered starts above 3.0)\n- **Internal relationship:** **none** \u2014 Caterpillar is not present in either the ERP Customer master or Vendor master (checked both, full substring search across all records), and not in Books either.\n\nOne thing worth flagging for the committee: leverage ticked down sharply in 2023 (equity jumped ~23% while debt fell slightly) then crept back up in 2024 as debt rose again \u2014 worth a sentence on trend volatility even though the classification itself is comfortably \"moderate.\"",
